cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ufi: a reference implementation of the Content Gap Score"
repository-code: "https://github.com/VenkataPagadalaGIT/ufi"
url: "https://github.com/VenkataPagadalaGIT/ufi"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pagadala
    given-names: Venkata
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
keywords:
  - content gap
  - information retrieval
  - knowledge graph
  - reproducibility
abstract: >
  Content gap scoring from industry structure and user questions. Implements
  the Content Gap Score at entity, relation and class level, the practitioner
  baselines it is compared against, and the reproducibility artifacts a study
  of it must publish: a frozen query set, a parameter lock, an auditable
  judgment cache and a run manifest. The score is a specification; no published
  study has yet tested whether it predicts anything.
